<<~ ahu #/group-b-bind-under-handle>>

!! GROUP B: `bind-under-handle.test.ts` red — gate correct, one caller unfed

`packages/lararium-node/tests/bind-under-handle.test.ts` fails with:

```
[daemon-keyhive] Binding Gate: current lease frontier unavailable — refusing persona-bound boot
```

''Cause.'' `dbb85cf63` (retire clock authority) made `expectedEpoch` a required parameter of
`bootDaemonKeyhive` (`packages/lararium-keyhive/src/boot-daemon-keyhive.ts:137`) and updated the two
callers it touched — but not the joinee boot path this test drives, which still calls in without
supplying the live lease epoch, so the gate correctly refuses.

''Fix direction (not applied by this hand — not this hand's files).'' Supply the live lease epoch the
same way `face-join.ts`'s `gateFaceJoin` already does for its own caller, rather than loosening or
bypassing the gate. The gate's refusal is doing its job here; the joinee boot path is the thing that
needs to catch up to it. Never revert or weaken the gate itself.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/held-out-workflow>>

!! `.github/workflows/held-out.yml` — a job-env `runner.temp` read fails every push

''What breaks.'' `held-out.yml:36` reads `runner.temp` inside a job-level `env:` block. `runner` context
is unavailable there — a job's `env:` block only sees `github`, `needs`, `strategy`, `matrix`, `vars`,
`secrets`, and `inputs` — so GitHub rejects the whole workflow file on every push as a 0s failure (for
example run `37309501567`). A schedule/workflow_dispatch-only file still gets validated on push; the
trigger named in the file does not exempt it from parse-time context checks.

''Fix (not applied by this hand — Codex hearth's hold).'' Delete the job-env `ARTIFACT_DIR` line, and in
the "Prepare held-out evidence directory" step compute the path inside a `run:` step instead, where the
`runner` context IS available:

```
run: |
  dir="$RUNNER_TEMP/held-out/${{ matrix.driver }}"
  mkdir -p "$dir"
  echo "ARTIFACT_DIR=$dir" >> "$GITHUB_ENV"
```

Later `$ARTIFACT_DIR` / `${{ env.ARTIFACT_DIR }}` uses then resolve against the step-exported value. This
hand did not touch `.github/workflows/held-out.yml` itself — it is held by the Codex hearth.

<<~/ahu>>

